Package: ofeIntegrateR
Title: Design, Sample and Analyse On-Farm Strip Experiments
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Zhanglong", "Cao", , "zhanglong.cao@curtin.edu.au", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A workflow for on-farm experimentation (OFE) strip trials,
    from planning a trial to estimating its treatment effects. Lays out strip
    and stacked designs with randomised or systematic treatment order; works
    out how many point samples a target precision needs and where to put them;
    aggregates irregular yield-monitor data onto an estimable lattice; and
    estimates treatment effects, optionally integrating a sparse point-source
    variable (soil cores, tissue tests) with the dense layer by a kriged
    covariate or a joint bivariate spatial model. Every step has an
    open-source path requiring no commercial software licence, with ASReml-R
    used automatically where it is licensed. Developed for the AAGI-CU-RD-OFE
    GRDC project.
